Article 13 If the addressee fails to sign for the judicial documents served by the People's Court, but any of the following circumstances exists, the service shall be deemed as having been effected:
(1) the addressee has mentioned in writing to the People's Court the content of the served judicial documents;
(2) the addressee has performed in accordance with the content of the served judicial documents;
(3) other circumstances under which service may be deemed as having been effected.
